6056994 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186056995 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186056994 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186056996 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186056994 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186056997 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186056994 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186056998 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186056994 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186056999 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186056994 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186056994 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186056994 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "c555a8be-5736-508c-a3a8-50d0c1ffb86f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186056995 #edb/ref 1080 "$3 \\mid 18$ and $11$ is not prime" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186056995 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186056995 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "d0035e6e-f36a-5da1-a062-615e7f0ab3c9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186056996 #edb/ref 1080 "$3 \\mid 18$ and $11$ is prime" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186056996 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186056996 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0b775ec8-6ca9-5db2-8064-a450b230418a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186056997 #edb/ref 1080 "$3⧸ \\mid 18$ and $11$ is prime" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186056997 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186056997 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "101774e8-84db-52ee-9a64-592220a96e3c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186056998 #edb/ref 1080 "$3⧸ \\mid 18$ or $11$ is prime" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186056998 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186056998 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "37228b0c-4acf-5470-b487-ce615401948e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186056999 #edb/ref 1080 "$3 \\mid 18$ or $11$ is prime" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186056999 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186056999 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "698ca85f-1919-5143-8622-5c257aae85d7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059403 #edb/ref 1069 "e-12694" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059403 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the negation of the following compound statement? \n\n$\\qquad$ $6$ is composite and $5\\!\\not{|} \\, 3.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059403 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "fc8d6c59-5351-5ca1-95e1-fa1470799bbc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059403 #edb/ref 1074 "De Morgan's law posits that the negation of a conjunction of two statements is equivalent to the disjunction of the negated individual statements. It can be stated symbolically as follows.\n\n$$\n\\neg ( A \\land B) = \\neg A \\lor \\neg B\n$$\n\nSo, the negation of our statement is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬(6\\text{ is composite}\\text{ and }5\\,\\text{⧸}|\\,3) & ≡¬((6\\text{ is composite})∧(5\\,\\text{⧸}|\\,3)) \\\\  & ≡¬(6\\text{ is composite})∨¬(5\\,\\text{⧸}|\\,3) \\\\  & ≡(6\\text{ is not composite})∨(5\\,|\\,3) \\\\  & ≡6\\text{ is not composite}\\text{ or }5\\,|\\,3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059404 #edb/ref 1069 "e-12695" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059404 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the negation of the following compound statement?\n\n$\\qquad$ $3$ is not prime or $\\pi$ is not rational." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059404 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4d1dc931-6a8c-53fc-abc7-369df54b0912" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059404 #edb/ref 1074 "De Morgan's law for disjunctions states that the negation of a disjunction of two statements is equivalent to the conjunction of the negations of the individual statements. It can be stated symbolically as follows:\n\n$$\n\\neg ( A \\lor B) = \\neg A \\land \\neg B.\n$$\n\nSo, the negation of our statement is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬(3\\text{ is not prime}\\text{ or }\\pi \\text{ is not rational}) & ≡¬((3\\text{ is not prime})∨(\\pi \\text{ is not rational})) \\\\  & ≡¬(3\\text{ is not prime})∧¬(\\pi \\text{ is not rational}) \\\\  & ≡(3\\text{ is prime})∧(\\pi \\text{ is rational}) \\\\  & ≡3\\text{ is prime}\\text{ and }\\pi \\text{ is rational}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059405 #edb/ref 1069 "e-12696" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059405 #edb/ref 1071 "Simplify the statement $\\neg ( (P \\lor \\neg Q) \\land (Q \\lor \\neg P) )$ using De Morgan's laws." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059405 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a3430492-73ee-5c65-92cf-7059bb63b5a4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059405 #edb/ref 1074 "De Morgan's laws state that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬(P∧Q)≡¬P∨¬Q, \\\\ ¬(P∨Q)≡¬P∧¬Q.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can simplify the given statement as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬((P∨¬Q)∧(Q∨¬P)) & ≡¬(P∨¬Q)∨¬(Q∨¬P) \\\\  & ≡(¬P∧¬(¬Q))∨(¬Q∧¬(¬P)) \\\\  & ≡(¬P∧Q)∨(¬Q∧P)\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059696 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048349 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059696 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048778 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059696 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186060105 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059696 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186060108 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059696 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186376254 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059696 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186376261 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059696 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186401695 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059696 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186401702 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059696 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186571388 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059696 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186571451 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059696 #edb/ref 1039 "Negating a Sentence Containing a Conjunction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059696 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186059403 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059696 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "d9de08e2-7bf6-5ab5-bb90-7f2896dda1dc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059697 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186060106 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059697 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186060107 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059697 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186376374 #edb/ref 17592